## 📚 Why RxDB Over Dexie.js (For Your Use Case)

You mentioned you'll build **live collaborative coding** (multiple people editing one file) in the future. This changes the recommendation:

| Feature | Dexie.js | RxDB | Why RxDB Wins for You |
|---------|----------|------|----------------------|
| **Reactive queries** | ❌ Manual | ✅ Built-in | Live collab needs instant UI updates when data changes |
| **Replication/Sync** | ❌ Build yourself | ✅ Built-in plugin | Multi-device + collaboration needs battle-tested sync |
| **Conflict resolution** | ❌ Build yourself | ✅ Built-in | Two users edit same note → RxDB handles merge |
| **Multi-tab support** | ⚠️ Limited | ✅ Leader election | Same user with 2 tabs open won't corrupt data |
| **Observable data** | ❌ No | ✅ RxJS streams | UI auto-updates when another collaborator makes a change |
| **Encryption** | ❌ No | ✅ Plugin | Sensitive notes encrypted at rest in browser |
| **Bundle size** | ~16KB | ~150KB | Acceptable trade-off for the features |

### How RxDB Works (Simple Explanation)

```javascript
// 1. Define your database schema (like Mongoose, but for the browser)
const noteSchema = {
  title: 'note',
  version: 0,
  primaryKey: 'id',
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    id:        { type: 'string', maxLength: 100 },
    title:     { type: 'string' },
    content:   { type: 'object' },           // your cell data
    folder:    { type: 'string' },
    isStarred: { type: 'boolean' },
    isTrashed: { type: 'boolean' },
    owner:     { type: 'string' },
    updatedAt: { type: 'number' },           // timestamp
    _deleted:  { type: 'boolean' }           // soft delete for sync
  },
  required: ['id', 'owner']
};

// 2. Create the database
const db = await createRxDatabase({
  name: 'zohonotes',
  storage: getRxStorageDexie()   // RxDB uses Dexie/IndexedDB under the hood!
});
await db.addCollections({ notes: { schema: noteSchema } });

// 3. CRUD is simple
await db.notes.insert({ id: 'note-1', title: 'Hello', ... });
const note = await db.notes.findOne('note-1').exec();
await note.patch({ title: 'Updated Title' });

// 4. REACTIVE — UI auto-updates (this is the magic for live collab)
db.notes.find().$.subscribe(allNotes => {
  renderNotesList(allNotes);  // Called automatically whenever ANY note changes
});

// 5. SYNC with Atlas (built-in replication)
const replicationState = replicateRxCollection({
  collection: db.notes,
  replicationIdentifier: 'notes-atlas-sync',
  pull: { handler: fetchNotesFromAtlas },
  push: { handler: pushNotesToAtlas },
  live: false,          // not constant live — we trigger manually
  retryTime: 10000,     // retry every 10s on failure
});
```

