## 🗂️ Data Flow: The Lazy-Load + Backup Strategy

You specified: *"Only required data in local. If user hasn't opened the data, fetch it and store locally. If local already has it, use local."*

Here's exactly how that works:

### On Login (First Time on This Device)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Browser as Browser (RxDB)
    participant Server as Render + Atlas

    User->>Browser: Opens app, logs in
    Browser->>Server: POST /api/auth/login
    Server-->>Browser: ✅ Auth token + user profile
    Browser->>Server: GET /api/sync/manifest
    Note right of Server: Returns lightweight list:<br/>[ {id, title, folder, updatedAt} ]<br/>NOT full content!
    Server-->>Browser: Note manifest (titles + metadata only)
    Browser->>Browser: Store manifest in RxDB<br/>(sidebar shows all note titles)
    Note over Browser: Full note content is NOT<br/>downloaded yet — lazy!
```

### When User Opens a Specific Note

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant RxDB as RxDB (Local)
    participant Server as Atlas (Cloud)

    User->>RxDB: Opens "My Python Notes"
    RxDB->>RxDB: Check: do I have full content?
    
    alt Content exists locally
        RxDB-->>User: ✅ Show from local (instant, < 5ms)
        RxDB->>Server: Background: check if cloud version is newer
        alt Cloud is newer
            Server-->>RxDB: Download updated content
            RxDB->>RxDB: Merge changes
            RxDB-->>User: ✅ Auto-refresh UI (RxDB reactive!)
        end
    else Content NOT in local
        RxDB->>Server: GET /api/sync/note/:id (fetch full content)
        Server-->>RxDB: Full note content
        RxDB->>RxDB: Store in IndexedDB
        RxDB-->>User: ✅ Show note
    end
```

### When User Saves/Edits a Note

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant RxDB as RxDB (Local)
    participant Sync as Sync Engine
    participant Atlas as Atlas (Cloud)

    User->>RxDB: Edits note (types, adds cell, etc.)
    RxDB->>RxDB: ✅ Saved to IndexedDB (instant, < 5ms)
    RxDB->>Sync: Notify: "note-123 changed"
    
    Note over Sync: Debounce 10 seconds<br/>(wait for user to stop typing)
    
    Sync->>Sync: User stopped typing for 10s
    
    alt Online
        Sync->>Atlas: POST /api/sync/push {note-123}
        Atlas-->>Sync: ✅ Backed up
    else Offline
        Sync->>Sync: Add to sync queue
        Note over Sync: Will retry when online
    end
```

