## 🔄 Multi-Device Conflict Resolution

Since you want multi-device support, two devices could edit the same note. Here's how we handle it:

### Conflict Strategy: "Last Write Wins" + "Merge When Possible"

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["User edits on Phone<br/>updatedAt: 10:30 AM"] -->|"Syncs to Atlas"| C["Atlas<br/>updatedAt: 10:30 AM"]
    B["User edits on Laptop<br/>updatedAt: 10:32 AM"] -->|"Syncs to Atlas"| D{"Conflict?"}
    C --> D
    
    D -->|"Different fields changed<br/>(title on phone, content on laptop)"| E["✅ Auto-merge both changes"]
    D -->|"Same field changed"| F["⚠️ Last-write-wins<br/>(laptop version kept,<br/>phone version archived)"]
    F --> G["📋 Conflict log shown to user<br/>'A version from your phone was replaced'"]
```

**RxDB has built-in conflict handling** — this is one of the reasons we chose it. We configure a custom conflict handler:

```javascript
// Conceptual — RxDB conflict handler
const conflictHandler = (input) => {
  const { newDocumentState, realMasterState, currentForkState } = input;
  
  // If the conflict is on different fields, merge them
  // If the conflict is on the same field, keep the newer timestamp
  // Archive the losing version in a "conflict_history" collection
  
  return {
    isEqual: false,
    documentData: resolvedVersion
  };
};
```

