## ⚠️ Remaining Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. **Should we keep the current Handlebars (server-rendered) views, or move to a client-side SPA framework (React/Vue)?** The local-first approach works best with a client-side SPA. Currently your views are server-rendered `.hbs` files. We can make it work with Handlebars, but a future SPA migration would be much cleaner for RxDB's reactive features.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 2. **For the live collaborative coding feature (future) — do you envision Google Docs-style real-time cursors, or is it more like Git-style "pull latest changes"?** This affects whether we need WebSockets + CRDT now or can add it later.

3. **Should we implement RxDB encryption for notes stored in IndexedDB?** It's free with RxDB but adds slight overhead. Useful if users store sensitive code/notes.

4. **Do you want a "version history" feature for notes?** (Ability to see and restore previous versions of a note.) It's easy to add with RxDB but adds storage usage.

